  "query_preview": "..\n\nA cold front associated with an upper-level trough digging over\neastern Montana will pass overnight. Winds will veer NW and \nincrease in magnitude following frontal passage. A Lake Wind \nAdvisory is currently being considered for tomorrow morning and\nafternoon. Precipitation is not anticipated.\n\nThe trough will rapidly exit eastward Thursday evening ahead of a\nstrong upper-level ridge building over the western United States.\nThe ridging pattern will produce warm and dry conditions Friday \nand Saturday.\n\nThe ridge will gradually translate eastward ahead of an\napproaching upper-level trough. Minor perturbations embedded \nwithin the resultant SW flow aloft may elevate winds slightly \nearly in the weekend, but no significant deviations from the \nridge-induced weather regime are expected.\n\nThe aforementioned trough is expected to weaken before digging \nover Montana by Sunday morning, resulting in daily high\ntemperatures in the low-to-mid 60s throughout the first half of \nnext week.\n\nFlow aloft over the central United States will back SW over the\ncourse of Monday as an Aleutian low digs southward, settling off\nthe coast of central California by Tuesday morning. Current model\nguidance indicates the atmosphere will be relatively dry during \nthis period. Little change to the perceptible weather is \nanticipated.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\n- There is high confidence in conditions remaining largely benign\n  throughout the forecast period.\n\n- No deviations from the NBM.\n\n\nDON",
